-- erwartet: C001
-- **645 -- a `static` array whose length no C object can have.**
--
-- `[u64; 2^63 - 1]` is accepted -- the length is a `u64` and fits. The emitter wrote it out
-- as the array bound and `cc` answered
--
--     size of array `A` exceeds maximum object size `9223372036854775807`
--
-- **`gift/602` is the neighbour, and the pair is the point.** That one carries the length the
-- emitter READ WRONG (`2^128 - 1` came back as `-1`, and the array was declared `[-1]`); this
-- one carries a length the emitter reads exactly right and writes into a C declaration that
-- cannot exist. *One is a lossy conversion, the other is a missing bound* -- and until
-- 2026-09-02 the same slot of the same grammar rule produced both.
--
-- Found by `instrumente/fuzze-erzeuger.py`: the `array-laenge` form gave 12 non-compiling
-- cases at the top of the ladder, and this is the lowest of them -- the last value that is
-- still an honest `u64`.
--
-- THE REPAIR, 2026-09-03 -- and the number in the refusal is C's, not a choice
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- A refusal, because C has no such object and there is nothing to lower to. **What the
-- refusal has to get right is WHICH limit**, and it is not the element count: C requires
-- the difference of two pointers into one object to be representable as a `ptrdiff_t`, so
-- the bound is on BYTES. `9223372036854775807` is `PTRDIFF_MAX`, and it is the number GCC
-- prints in its own message -- read off that message rather than assumed.
--
-- So the emitter multiplies the length by the width of the element type and compares. An
-- element whose width it cannot name counts as **one byte**, the smallest any C object
-- has: the rule then under-refuses rather than over-refuses, and what it lets through `cc`
-- still catches. *The safe direction is the one where the second reader is still there.*
--
-- > **A neighbour this repair did NOT close, and it is worse than what it did close.**
-- > `static mut A : [u64; 100000000] = 7;` -- a hundred million, well inside `PTRDIFF_MAX`
-- > -- makes `gabbro emit` run without end: a non-zero initialiser is written out element
-- > by element, on purpose (`= {5}` in C means *first five, rest zero*, which is not what
-- > Gabbro's `= 5` means). Measured 2026-09-03: killed at 25 s with an empty output file.
-- > **That is the emitter's third answer -- neither a lowering nor a refusal -- and the
-- > sweep that found the six counted zero of those.** It is left open here rather than
-- > fenced with an invented number.

module gift::array_longer_than_c_can_object_to {

static mut A : [u64; 9223372036854775807] = 0;

}
